  ---
  duration_ms: 0.431247
  type: 'test'
  ...
# Subtest: injectFormSubmissionResultIntoHtml: a double-quoted value="Don't know" containing an apostrophe is REPLACED, not duplicated -- bug (e): the 2026-09-05 fix's own existing-attribute check, /(\\s)value=(["'])[^"']*\\2/i, excludes BOTH quote characters from the value body, so it cannot span an embedded apostrophe inside a double-quoted value and never matches at all here -- the code falls through to the append branch and adds a second value=, and the browser honors only the first (the stale "Don't know")
